			"Message": "build(Mountain): Revert production profile names to simple Mountain identifier\n\nComplete the reversion of verbose production build profile names back to simplified \"Mountain\" naming. Update Cargo.toml binary, library, and default-run targets to use \"Mountain\" instead of the full production profile string. Update tauri.conf.json productName and identifier to match, and remove the duplicate \"Binary/node\" entry from externalBin. Also delete the now-redundant Cargo.toml.Backup and tauri.conf.json.Backup files.\n\nThis aligns with the simplified naming scheme for both development and production builds, reducing configuration complexity while maintaining the multi-profile build pipeline functionality.",
			"SHA": "20b936312a943ce8be8f0a2837225f346b5715af"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T05:07:51Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				870,
				4
			],
			"Message": "build(Mountain): Update binary/lib names and Tauri config for production build profile\n\nRename the Mountain binary and library to include the full production environment profile string (ProductionNodeEnvironment_MicrosoftVSCodeDependency_22NodeVersion_Bundle_Clean_Compile_ElectronProfile_EsbuildCompiler_Mountain) to distinguish this build variant from development builds. Update tauri.conf.json productName and identifier to match, and add Binary/node to externalBin for the production node path.\n\nThis configuration supports the multi-profile build pipeline for distinguishing between development and production environment builds.",
			"SHA": "16bcfef9901bc9c03390b960918014975f74e4aa"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T04:54:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				868,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Add explicit font MIME type mappings for WKWebView\n\nWKWebView is strict about font MIME types - when the asset resolver falls back to `application/octet-stream` for `.ttf` files (which `infer` does on some macOS versions because TrueType has no magic header), the browser silently refuses to use the font. The workbench then renders icons as blank squares with no console error.\n\nAdd explicit MIME type mappings for TTF, OTF, WOFF, WOFF2, and EOT extensions in LocalhostPlugin::MimeFromUrl. This ensures the codicon font and extension assets under `/Static/Application/extensions/...` (KaTeX, Seti) render correctly in the workbench.",
			"SHA": "27cc378d013ac38b2c2ca0f9c8dc5fd75759a3c8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T02:41:11Z",
